{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation complete; Gerrit change https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2408 pushed (commit 6701a831b38f).\n\nWHAT CHANGED\n- _operation_config.py: contextvar-backed active-operation binding (active_snapshot / bind_operation_snapshot / compose_and_bind_operation_snapshot), composes exactly once per operation, reused by nested seams, fails OPEN on composition error. Added bind_operation_snapshot_for_tools(mcp), an MCP tool-registrar proxy mirroring _lib_warn.suppress_library_double_advisory's pattern.\n- config.py: tracker_dir/tickets_branch/tickets_remote consult the bound snapshot (new _bound_snapshot_for_root helper) before falling back to load_config, freezing them for the life of a bound operation. REBAR_TRACKER_DIR env override and an explicit different-repo root both still bypass the binding (AC3).\n- _cli/__init__.py: _main_dispatch composes-and-binds one snapshot around the store-mount gate + dispatch (replaces emit_shadow_snapshot(surface=\"cli\")).\n- _commands/_seam.py: append_event (the single command-write seam shared by CLI/MCP/Python) composes-and-binds reentrantly; body moved into _append_event_body.\n- mcp_server.py: build_server wires bind_operation_snapshot_for_tools around register_read_tools/register_write_tools only (not LLM tools).\n- _mcp_reads.py / _mcp_writes.py: deleted all 34 + 24 per-tool _shadow(...) call sites and the _shadow import.\n\nOUT OF SCOPE, documented and tested as deliberate carve-outs:\n- Push mode (_store/push.py, config.resolve_push_mode) stays LIVE per-call: _io/import_ndjson.py toggles REBAR_SYNC_PUSH mid-bulk-import and test_c3b_push_defer_coupling_heldout.py depends on that. Asserted explicitly by the new tests (push mode observes a mutation even inside a bound operation).\n- LLM-specific resolution (_mcp_llm.py, _lib_ops.py's bridge/reconciler ops, _engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py) keeps its shadow calls — that migration is ticket ec44.\n\nTDD EVIDENCE (held-out discipline, RED-first)\n- New tests/interfaces/contracts/test_operation_snapshot_authoritative_binding.py (9 tests): compose-once/reentrancy (CLI, command-write, MCP wrapper), tracker dir/branch/remote freeze vs. a fresh operation, AC3 env-override + cross-repo bypass, push-mode carve-out stays live, an E2E CLI ticket-create binding one real snapshot, and a fail-open litmus (a genuinely ConfigError-raising project config still lets `bridge setup --reset` succeed).\n- Genuine RED proof: `git stash push -- src/rebar` (implementation removed, new test file kept, untracked) -> new test file fails with `ImportError: cannot import name 'active_snapshot'` (a real absence-of-behavior failure, not a stub/assertion failure) -> `git stash pop` restored.\n- Mutation-teeth proof: live-mutated `_bound_snapshot_for_root` in config.py to force it to always return None (simulating \"never bound\") -> the two freeze tests (tracker_dir/tickets_branch/tickets_remote unchanged under mutation) correctly went RED -> restored the correct implementation (re-verified via full test rerun, 36 passed) after an incident where `git checkout --` on the uncommitted file briefly discarded the whole implementation (recovered by hand re-derivation, then re-validated).\n- Litmus (behavior-preserving-refactor immunity): all new assertions are on observable behavior only (CLI stdout/exit code, config.py's public tracker_dir/tickets_branch/tickets_remote return values, real fail-open success) — no internal structure/private-attribute assertions.\n- tests/unit/test_single_definition_helpers.py updated (existing held-out oracle for _shadow's single-definition invariant): now asserts _mcp_reads/_mcp_writes no longer import _shadow at all (new positive-migration test), while the original guarantee is preserved for the still-unmigrated _mcp_llm/_lib_ops.\n\nVALIDATION\n- make lint: fully green (ruff check + format, complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0, check_config_ownership.py clean with zero new legacy exceptions, env-vars.md registry regenerated and current, zizmor, shellcheck, etc.)\n- make typecheck: clean, 698 source files, zero errors.\n- make test: 18083+ non-skipped tests, all green except 8 pre-existing failures (test_atomic_completion_close.py x5, test_rebar_repo_isolation.py::test_copy_repoints_sibling_origin_and_keeps_refs_isolated, test_tracker_footprint_cli.py x2). Confirmed pre-existing/unrelated: reproduced identically with `git stash push -- src/rebar` (this ticket's implementation removed) and again after `git stash pop`. Not fixed here — out of scope, matching the precedent set by prior ticket 02b7-82ef-ca69-4aa8 in this epic.\n- Rebased cleanly onto 6 newer origin/main commits (unrelated: eval budget ledger, Bedrock model pinning, plan-review corpus builder, a release, retryable-disposition fallback, ADR 0107) — confirmed zero file overlap with this ticket's Scope before fast-forwarding; re-ran lint/typecheck/key test files post-rebase, all green.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA: all 7 checked off in the description above, each with a one-line pointer to its proof.\n\nfile_impact widened to the 10 actually-changed files/paths (rebar set-file-impact).\n\nNext: awaiting Gerrit LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 on change 2408 before transitioning this ticket to closed and submitting."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788063110534525001,"uuid":"f17682b1-1599-461f-9151-d468c9453f48"}